  "body": "An external AI reviewed the Reference Agent's runtime logs and flagged two real problems behind a lot of scary-looking log noise. Verified against the code \u2014 the Python framework (`mantle/`) was already correct; the bugs were in the demo(s).\n\n## A \u2014 Noisy correction/retry loop (the alarming `SYS.CORRECT` clusters)\nThe cognitive loop forced up to two retries whenever the model returned no tool call \u2014 **even for ordinary conversation** \u2014 while `tool_choice=\"auto\"` let the model legitimately answer in prose. Now **event-gated**: `requiresTool = hb || wantsBodyChange`. A plain chat turn is accepted as-is (no `SYS.CORRECT`, no retry); the integrity check still fires for heartbeats and for a model that *claims* a body/UI change it didn't execute. The arm path likewise only nudges when the Arm returned nothing usable.\n\n## B \u2014 Genome body-entries vanished on reload (`<bodyentry.000/.001/.003> missing-bodyentry` every call)\n`s.bodyEntries` was **never serialized into the crystal nor restored on load**. Now the Body genome (+ `genesisKey` + `scheduledPulses`) round-trips through save/load, **self-heals** a missing immutable primer on load (`ensureGenomeEntries`), is guaranteed present across the awakening, and `MODEL.REQUEST` `bodyRefs` are built from **populated slots only** (`activeBodyRefs`) \u2014 so an empty inheritance slot never tombstones.\n\n## C \u2014 Dangling refs mislabeled `unsupported-reference-syntax`\n`<facts.11>` / `<gen0.facts.0>` are **valid syntax** (the demo's `parseRef` *and* `mantle/core/refs.py` support them) but **dangling** on a sparse cube. They now read as `dangling-reference` (mirroring `refs.py`: dangling \u2192 immune event), deduped within a stable cube so a phantom ref stuck in chat history doesn't re-fire forever. *(The reviewer's claim that the JS resolver didn't support the syntax was incorrect \u2014 the framework was right all along.)*\n\n**Spreadsheet:** already persisted `bodyEntries`, had no forced-tool loop, and used one honest `RECALL_ERROR` label \u2014 only its `MODEL.REQUEST` `bodyRefs` trace was made populated-slots-only.\n\n## Framework guard\nNew invariant **HF-B02 `t_body_genome_round_trip`** asserts the Body genome survives `to_dict`/`from_dict` (the exact contract the demo violated); the existing **HF-B24** already locks dangling \u2192 immune. Both demos' Stage-1 self-audits assert Genome/bodyRefs coherence (Reference Agent gains a `B-GEN` row; the Spreadsheet already checked all four slots + primer). Count **67 \u2192 68**; README + audit docs + `MOLT_LEDGER` updated (DOCTOR-1 enforces this).\n\n## Verification\n- **Browser:** both demos mount, zero runtime errors; Genome present after load; persistence round-trip survives; `bodyRefs` drop emptied slots (4\u21923); `<facts.11>`/`<gen0.*>` labeled `dangling-reference`, unknown band still `unsupported-reference-syntax`; `B-GEN` PASS; Spreadsheet self-audit PASS.\n- **Framework:** `python -m mantle prove` \u2192 **68/68 green** (incl. DOCTOR-1), Stage-1 audit PASS, teach PASS, three tamper proofs exit non-zero.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
